# One line ending everywhere: LF in the repository AND in every checkout.
# With core.autocrlf=true and no rule, checkouts were CRLF while agents wrote
# LF, so files ended up mixed (exact-match edits failed on them) and every
# `git add` printed a CRLF warning per file. Windows scripts keep CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
